-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

	Kfingerd-0.07 has just been released. For those of you who don't
know what Kfingerd is, it's a replacement for in.fingerd with significant
additional functionality. If you are using a version before 0.04, you _must_
upgrade. If you are using 0.04 or later, you _should_ upgrade.

	Features include user control over what information is released
about them, programmed response rather than fixed files, and 'subnames' that
allow users to vary the response to fingers based upon information provided
by the fingerer.

	This release fixes several bugs in the code that computes time
offsets in the tty display. Kfingerd also now works properly with newer
utmps. A bug that could have caused wildly inaccurate login and idle times
to be displayed for console logins was fixed. Kfingerd also now properly
deals with some obscure versions of finger that pass options in an obscure
way.

	To see a tiny demo of what Kfingerd can do, finger
'dalnet@cyberplus.com'. This will also give you a list of servers for
DALnet IRC, where you usually find the author (JoelKatz) and ask him
questions about Kfingerd. 

