This is to announce a new version of taper. Taper is a user friendly
backup program for Linux. It supports floppy and SCSI tape drives,
as well as QIC-02 (in alpha stage) tapes. Multi-tape archives,
incremental backups and most-recent restore options are supported.

Files are selected via a user-friendly interface, similar to that
of Norton Commander (or Mouseless Commander). This version includes
support for unattended backups.


