Among other things, the 2.1 release contains the following improvements:

* Simplified Installation

The installation process has been trimmed and streamlined.  The
differences between the 5 types of installation (CD-ROM, NFS, FTP,
floppy disk, and hard drive) have been minimized, resulting in less
confusion and clearer installation instructions in the manual.

* Expanded Manual

Notwithstanding some heavy editing and cruft-cutting, the manual has
grown over 25 pages -- to 147 pages.  Additional sections cover
upgrading from 2.0; configuring sendmail, tcpd, anonymous ftp, World
Wide Web services, and NFS; and finding documentation.

* New Installation Modes

Red Hat Linux 2.1 now supports installations from the following sources:

	. CD-ROM
	. NFS
	. FTP
	. Floppy disks
	. DOS (or other) partition

