Date: 1995/11/23
Message-ID: <cola-liw-817158465-20201-1@oravannahka.helsinki.fi>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 120008134
followup-to: comp.os.linux.development.system
content-type: text/plain; charset=ISO-8859-1
organization: Gerhard-Mercator-Universitaet -GH- Duisburg
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.os.linux.announce

-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

DMSDOS is a filesystem extension to the msdos filesystem for Linux.
Mount Msdos 6.0, Msdos 6.2 doublespace, Msdos 6.22 drivespace and Win95
doublespace compressed partitions under Linux with the dmsdos filesystem.

Dmsdos features:

 * all compressed volume files are converted to subdirectories where you
   can find the complete compressed filesystem
 * full read access, restricted write access to compressed partitions
 * supports compressed floppies
 * can coexist with umsdos in the same partition
 * can use umsdos extensions in compressed partitions
 * when writing, a compression level may be selected by the user
 * supports standard (like msdos driver) and extended (cp 437) text conversion
 * supports old Win95 doublespace

Currently unsupported, but under construction:

 - Win95 drivespace 3 support
 - *very* new Linux kernels > 1.3.38 (?)

Recommended Linux kernel to use with dmsdos: 1.2.13 or 1.3.24 

Note: This is not the software you want if you want to compress Linux data
(it works in an umsdos partition, but it's too slow).

Sites:
  sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/system/Filesystems/dosfs
  74 kb dmsdosfs-0.5.8.tgz

  ftp.uni-stuttgart.de /pub/systems/linux/local/system
  74 kb dmsdosfs-0.5.8.tgz

If you don't find the files, try the Incoming directories.


