i've created a CGI browser for the Linux kernel source.  It
attempts to do the following:

	* Format ANSI C keywords in <B>bold</B>.
	* Format comments in <I>italics</I>
	* Turn #include directives into links
	* Turn functions and variables into links to their
	  corresponding definitions (this is a REALLY great way
	  to understand the code, but some of the links lead to
	  unexpected places - ie alpha definitions instead of
	  ix86 and other such things.  This is due to the way
	  I indexed the functions and will be fixed sometime)
	* Display README files for directories + allow directory
	  browsing

  Check it out as:

