The University of California at Berkeley's Linux Users Group, (CalLUG)
is meeting on

WEDNESDAY, DECEMBER 6, 7pm
HP Auditorium (room 306), UC Berkeley

This meeting is timed to accompany the DECUS '95/SF conference, which
includes a large Linux trade show and a number of Linux-based
presentations.  We will have a report from the conference, followed by
a talk from DECUS '95 speaker Phil Hughes, publisher of Linux Journal,
entitled "Publishing and the Linux Market".  This talk, given last
year at DECUS '94/Washington DC, includes an overview of the use of
Unix and Linux in paper/software/CD/magazine publishing over the past
10 years, how Linux Journal/SSC use this technology now, and the
future of Linux and publishing.

ATTENDING THE MEETING:

All are welcome at the meeting, including new Linux users or non Linux 
users, and people unaffiliated with the University or CalLUG.  

Soda Hall is located on the north side of the UC Berkeley campus.  The
nearest cross streets are LeRoy and Hearst.  Parking is available for
$3 (quarters only) in the garage at Hearst and La Loma after 6pm.
Street parking is also available for free after 6pm.  Links to
directions to campus via car and public transportation, as well as
maps to locate the building, are available at:
<URL:http://www-callug.cs.berkeley.edu/directions.html>

This meeting is wheelchair accessible.  
If you have any questions, send mail to board@callug.cs.berkeley.edu.


FUTURE CALLUG MEETINGS:

CalLUG is always interested in hearing from people who have ideas for
future presentations or who would like to speak on behalf of a
Linux-related corporation or group.  Send mail to
board@callug.cs.berkeley.edu or find additional details on our home
page.
 
