I have created a small program to show the queue of packets and their Time
To Live for the proxy interface provided by the diald (v0.11) package.  It
has the aura of top to it, and although it is in a very rudimentary stage,
I have seen a lot of interest is out there for this program (as is 
evidenced by the response I got to my mailing to the linux-diald mailing
list.

The program requires ncurses libraries to compile, and seems to work well
for me.  I would appreciate any and all feedback I can get.  If you have
additions/hacks/etc to the program, please mail me diffs of what you have
done, and I will try to work it in to the later revisions.

Right now the code all resides in the mainline (it took me about 3 hours to get
it to where it is now -- most of this was reading up on ncurses)...  I have
several improvements in mind, but other input is always appreciated.

I have uploaded the archive and the LSM to sunsite (it is currently in the
/pub/Linux/Incoming directory -- I expect it to be moved with diald which
resides in /pub/Linux/system/Network/serial.


