KL Group Inc. is now shipping all of its XRT widgets, XRT/3d,
     XRT/field, XRT/graph and XRT/table, on the Linux operating system.
     This move enables developers using Linux to include the
     market-leading XRT family of widgets in their applications. Linux
     is a freely-distributable version of Unix that continues to enjoy
     growth in popularity among developers.

     XRT widgets for Linux are approximately half of the standard Unix
     prices. Prices for a single development license in North America
     are as follows:

        * XRT/graph - $995
        * XRT/3d    - $1,245
        * XRT/table - $745
        * XRT/field - $495

     There are no royalty or run-time fees for distributing end-user
     applications built with XRT products.

     Greg Kiessling, president of KL Group said, "The rapid growth of
     the Linux community has been astounding. We're pleased to be one
     of the first software tools vendors to offer
     commercially-supported versions of our products on this popular
     operating system."

     Bob Young, president of Red Hat Software Inc., builder of the
     leading Red Hat Linux distribution, stated, "KL Group's decision
     to port to Linux is proof of the commercial use of the Linux
     operating system. Linux developers will now be able to incorporate
     advanced widget technology into their applications quickly and
     easily. These components will not only save developers a
     significant amount of time, but they will also benefit end users
     by enabling them to interpret information based on the visual
     display of data."

     Steve Rosenberg, vice president of software engineering, KL Group,
     said "the addition of Linux to the list of supported operating
     systems and architectures for the XRT product line brings the
     total number of supported platforms to fifteen. KL Group is
     constantly adding new operating systems to its list of supported
     platforms, and will be continuing to increase the number that XRT
     products are available on. By supporting Linux, KL Group moves one
     step closer toward our corporate goal of providing all developers,
     regardless of the O/S they use, with the ability to incorporate
     our XRT widgets into their applications."

About the Companies

     KL Group is a leading supplier of software objects for GUI
     development for X Window System developers. XRT products are sold
     and supported from KL Group's corporate headquarters in Toronto,
     Canada, and through a worldwide network of qualified resellers.
     The company is located at 260 King Street East, Third Floor,
     Toronto, Ontario, Canada M5A 1K3.

     For more information about the XRT widgets or to get a free
     30-day evaluation, contact info@klg.com or visit
