From: Kurt Reisler <klr@bearzden.com>
Subject: DECUS SF to feature special Linux technical track
Date: 1995/11/09
Message-ID: <ann-6583.815893434@cs.cornell.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 118926923
approved: linux-announce@news.ornl.gov (Matt Welsh)
sender: mdw@cs.cornell.edu
followup-to: comp.os.linux.misc
organization: None
keywords: DECUS, Technical conference, Linux track, San Francisco
reply-to: Kurt Reisler <klr@bearzden.com>
newsgroups: comp.os.linux.announce,comp.os.linux.misc,comp.os.linux.advocacy,comp.os.linux.setup,comp.os.linux.development.system

Following two successful Linux special tracks (in New Orleans in 1994
and Washington DC in 1995) the US Chapter of DECUS is in the process of
setting up another Linux special track in conjunction with its Fall 1995
symposium, scheduled for December 2-7 1995, at the Moscone Center in San
Francisco.  This special track will be held December 6th and 7th in the
Marriott Hotel, with registration in the Moscone Center nearby.

The Linux Daze event will feature Matt Welsh, Coordinator of the Linux
Documentation Project, and author of two books on Linux as the keynote
speaker.  In addition, we are planning on having speakers from many of
the major commercial firms providing software and hardware support to
the Linux effort, including Cyclades, Craftwork and Digital.  We are
also planning on having a Linux vendor area which will include the
following; O'Reilly, Cyclades, Craftwork, Red Hat, Linux Journal, SSC
and several others.

We are planning on two half-day seminars on December 6th.  These
seminars are entitled "Linux: The Open System for Everyone" (by Phil
Hughes), and "Writing a Linux Device Driver: A Technical Introduction"
(by Michael K. Johnson).

Registration for the seminars costs $150 and is separate from the
regular DECUS seminars.

In addition, from 7 p.m. to 9 p.m., on the evening of the 6th, Matt
Welsh will be giving a FREE lecture entitled "Porting UNIX Applications
to Linux", sponsored by O'Reilly Books.  This presentation is free to
the general public and will be held in the Marriott hotel, with no
registration required.

The Linux technical sessions will include, in addition to a keynote
address by Matt Welsh, sessions on Linux and the Alpha CPU architecture,
using freeware operating systems in teaching, Linux in a commercial
setting, building an Internet server with Linux, using Linux to build a
webserver and bastion host, protecting your Linux system with a UPS and
using the UNIX shell as a 4GL.  In addition, there will be several
UNIX-related presentations at the DECUS symposium which may be of
interest to members of the Linux community.

An expected highlight of this special Linux track will be related to the
Linux running an a DEC Alpha PC.  If you attended the Linux sessions in
Washington DC, you had an opportunity to see a developmental version of
Linux running on a "no name" 166MHz Alpha PC.  At the San Francisco
event, you will have the opportunity to not only see the final version,
but you will also be able to purchase complete DEC Alpha Linux systems.
We anticipate that we will have CDROM distributions available from at
least one vendor.

Cost of the Linux technical track is only $40 and is separate from the
general symposium registration.

If you are planning on attending the entire DECUS Conference, you should
be aware that the early bird registration deadline is November 10th.  If
you would like additional information, you can check the Linux track
page on the DECUS US Chapter home page at

	  http://www.decus.org/decus/events/95sanfran/linux.html

Remember that this event is still being firmed up, and the information
on the home page may not necessarily be complete.

You can obtain a PostScript version of the registration form from the
DECUS home page (http://www.decus.org/decus) or via FTP from
FTP.DECUS.ORG under [decus95-sanfran] as reg.ps

For more information regarding Linux on the DEC Alpha, please see URL:

		http://www.azstarnet.com/~axplinux/

-- 
			  Kurt Reisler
		        klr@bearzden.com
		     Journeyman Linux Hacker		
		   Captain, UNIX SIG Luge Team

